//? Title: R-CNN region classification and box refinement
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Proposed object regions can recognize the right object while locating its edges poorly. This report fits a tensor patch CNN with class-specific box regression, showing padded warps, assignment masks and the complete Adam loop, then measures the same held-out predictions with and without learned refinement.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.6_object_detection/rcnn.cpp`.

> The method

R-CNN computes convolutional features separately for each proposed image patch. Classification identifies the object; a class-specific four-coordinate regressor corrects the proposal. The source teaching adaptation jointly learns softmax and regression heads on compact MNIST scenes rather than reproducing the original pretrained CNN/SVM/ridge pipeline.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/rcnn_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/rcnn_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/rcnn_concept.tikz > build/rcnn_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/rcnn_concept.svg build/rcnn_concept.dvi > build/rcnn_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
