Top: first four training scenes with green truth boxes. Bottom: identical pixels with all tight-threshold red proposals, including pair unions.
\image(figures/rcnn_proposals.png)
// result_end
\caption(The same four training images appear twice: green ground truth above and red component proposals below. The proposals include overlapping component pairs and can be too tight or merged.)
\alttext(The same four training images appear twice: green ground truth above and red component proposals below. The proposals include overlapping component pairs and can be too tight or merged.)

Each training scene contributes every proposal followed by every ground-truth
box. Maximum IoU selects the target, with first-target tie breaking. IoU at least
.5 gives its digit label; lower overlap means background class 10. Regression
uses only candidates reaching .6. Thus a region can be a foreground classification
example while its regressor is masked out. Appended truth boxes provide exact
positive examples with zero target offsets. Background and masked-out regression
targets are zero. The sampler performs no optimization or class balancing.

